# Local scratch.  Move unwanted-but-not-deletable files here: reference/ is
# ignored, so nothing in it reaches the repository, and nothing is destroyed.
reference/
v2/

# Downloaded datasets (run experiments/download_cifar.py to fetch)
cifar/

# Experiment outputs.
#
# `outputs/*` rather than `outputs/`: ignoring the DIRECTORY would make git skip
# it entirely, and no `!` negation inside it could ever take effect.  Ignoring the
# CONTENTS lets the evidence below be tracked while caches and legacy reports stay
# out.
#
# Tracked on purpose (FINDINGS.md cites these as its evidence; without them a
# fresh clone has a conclusions page pointing at files that do not exist):
#   outputs/abl_*.txt    ablation reports  (sections 5, 6, 8, 11)
#   outputs/abl_*.png    their figures
#   outputs/sub_01_*     the substrate verification suite (sections 2, 3, 8)
# Everything else under outputs/ is ignored: outputs/abl_cache/ (137 model
# caches), outputs/acl_diag/, and the legacy eNN_* reports, which are the live
# outputs of the older experiment scripts -- experiments/cifar_07_4d_rgb.py READS
# outputs/e18_digital_physical_report.txt, so those must not be moved or deleted.
# The patterns below are ANCHORED with a leading slash on purpose.  Unanchored,
# `outputs/*` and its negations match a directory named `outputs` at ANY depth,
# so `experiments/outputs/abl_something.txt` would have been whitelisted too.
# Verified with `git check-ignore -v`: an unanchored negation did let a nested
# copy through.  Anchoring keeps the whitelist to the repository's own outputs/.
/outputs/*
!/outputs/abl_*.txt
!/outputs/abl_*.png
!/outputs/sub_01_*.txt
# Added when the missing artifacts were found: five scripts PRINTED their results and saved
# nothing, so their numbers existed only in a terminal, and the CIFAR line's flagship number
# lived in an untracked report that a comparison script then HARD-CODED.  A number that
# cannot be cited cannot be checked, which is what made the CIFAR comparison unresolvable
# (extension FINDINGS.md 12.32).  These are tracked for the reason stated above -- the
# documents cite them -- and the e21 report is the one 12.32 quotes.
!/outputs/nd_*_report.txt
!/outputs/e21_regularized_report.txt
# The UNSEEDED report is kept as well, because it is the record of what was PUBLISHED
# before the seed was fixed -- and the two differ by 3.3 points, which is the finding.
!/outputs/e21_regularized_report_UNSEEDED.txt
# THE CIFAR LINE'S EVIDENCE, added when section 9's entry was written and its own citations
# turned out not to exist in a fresh clone -- the precise defect that entry is about.  Both
# sides are needed: the PRE_SEED files are the PUBLISHED values its table quotes, and the
# reports are the SEEDED ones that replace them.
!/outputs/e18_digital_physical_report.txt
!/outputs/e18_digital_physical_report_PRE_SEED.txt
!/outputs/e22_reg_3layer_peak_report.txt
!/outputs/e22_reg_3layer_peak_report_PRE_SEED.txt
!/outputs/e23_large_reg_4layer_report.txt
!/outputs/e23_large_reg_4layer_report_PRE_SEED.txt
!/outputs/e24_mlp_baseline_report.txt
!/outputs/e24_mlp_baseline_report_PRE_SEED.txt
!/outputs/e25_compare_report.txt
!/outputs/e25_compare_report_PRE_SEED.txt
!/outputs/sub_01_*.png

# The EXTENSION's evidence set (DESIGN section 9.2).  Without these lines the
# extension's reports are ignored and its conclusions would cite files that a
# clone cannot see -- the same defect that was fixed for the base version above.
!/outputs/ext_*.txt
!/outputs/ext_*.png

# Four STALE ablation-A figures, ignored BY NAME rather than by widening the rule
# above.  No script in the repository emits a `_smoke` or a non-`_shareaxis` plot
# name any more, and a repository-wide search finds these four cited in no
# document -- so they are orphans of an earlier version of
# experiments/abl_01_capacity_split.py.  The figures FINDINGS.md actually cites
# (abl_01_scaling_diffusion_shareaxis_plot.png and
# abl_01_capacity_split_diffusion_shareaxis_plot.png) are tracked and must stay
# so: a clone that cannot see them has a conclusions page pointing at files that
# do not exist, which is the defect the whitelist above exists to prevent.
# These patterns come AFTER the `!` negations on purpose -- a later pattern wins.
/outputs/abl_01_capacity_split_plot.png
/outputs/abl_01_scaling_plot.png
/outputs/abl_01_capacity_split_diffusion_smoke_plot.png
/outputs/abl_01_scaling_diffusion_smoke_plot.png

# The extension keeps its OWN model cache.  It must never write into
# outputs/abl_cache/: that cache is keyed by (task, arch, arm, seed, epochs,
# budget) and ablation C LOADS from it to reuse ablation A's models, so a
# colliding key would make abl_03 evaluate an extension model as if it were a
# base model (DESIGN section 9.1).  Covered by /outputs/* already; written out
# so nobody "tidies" it away.
outputs/ext_cache/

# experiments/cifar_07_4d_rgb.py resolves its OUT_DIR relative to itself, so when
# it is run from inside experiments/ it writes here instead of outputs/.  That
# script is not tracked yet (its inclusion was never decided), so neither are its
# artefacts -- ignore them rather than leaving two permanently-untracked files.
experiments/outputs/

test_outputs/

